  "question": {
    "text": "If <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mo>&#38;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>g</mi></math> are differentiable functions in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>]</mo><mo>&#160;</mo></math>satisfying <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mn>0</mn></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>=</mo><mi>g</mi><mfenced><mn>1</mn></mfenced><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>g</mi><mfenced><mn>0</mn></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#38;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mn>1</mn></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo></math> then for some <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>c</mi><mo>&#8712;]0,&#160;1[</mo></math>&nbsp;",
