  "solution": {
    "text": "Let <math><mi>h</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mi>f</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>g</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> clearly <math><mi>h</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>0</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mi>h</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced></math><br /><br />Also <math><mi>h</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> is continuous and differentiable.<br /><br />Hence <math><mi>h</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> satisfy all conditions of Rolle&#39;s theorem in <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>&#160;</mi><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>. According to Rolle&#39;s theorem there exist atleast one <math><mi>c</mi><mo>&#8712;</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>&#160;</mi><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> such that <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>h</mi><mo>'</mo></msup><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&#8658;</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>'</mo></msup><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><msup><mi>g</mi><mo>'</mo></msup><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math><br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>'</mo></msup><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mi>c</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><msup><mi>g</mi><mo>'</mo></msup><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mi>c</mi></mfenced></math>.",
